3 | Lists 5 skill groups |\n| Skills summary (all 13) | CLAUDE.md lines 142-158 | Lists all individual sub-skills |\n| Git commit convention | README.md lines 135-141 AND CLAUDE.md lines 160-167 | Nearly identical content |\n| Adding new skills | README.md lines 143-152 | 6-step process |\n| Design highlights | README.md lines 154-161 | 6 bullet points |\n| Documentation links | README.md lines 163-169 | Links to claude-code-cli-doc subdirectories |\n| Open issues | README.md lines 171-175 | 3 tracked issues |\n| Behavioral guidelines | CLAUDE.md lines 169-233 | Generic Claude Code guidelines (Part 2) |\n| Chinese documentation library | claude-code-cli-doc/ (130+ files) | Self-contained, has its own README |\n| GitHub templates | .github/ (7 files) | Issue/PR/Discussion templates in Chinese |\n| Skill output (drafts/templates) | doc/issues/ (10 files) | Generated by skills, not source material |"}]},{"tool_name":"Agent","tool_input":{"description":"Explore hooks and skills implementation","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"I need to understand the actual implementation details of the hooks system and skill system in this project at D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk, because I'll be writing mechanism documentation about them.\n\nPlease explore:\n\n1. **Hooks implementation** - Read `.claude/hooks/base.sh` (public infrastructure), `.claude/hooks/platform.sh`, and `.claude/settings.json` (to see how hooks are registered). Also check `.claude/hooks/01-session-start/base.sh` and `.claude/hooks/03-user-prompt-submit/base.sh` and `skill-inject.sh`.\n\n2. **Skill system** - Read `.claude/skills/registry.conf`, `.claude/skills/active.sh`, `.claude/skills/log.sh`. Check if there's a `lock.sh` file. Look at the actual skill directories to understand the pattern.\n\n3. **Init system** - Read `.claude/init.sh` and `.claude/dirs.conf`.\n\n4. **Scripts** - Read `.claude/scripts/ensure_dirs.sh`.\n\nReport the key implementation details: how hooks dispatch, how skills inject context, how initialization works, how locking works, how logging works. These details are needed for writing `docs/mechanisms/` documentation."},"tool_use_id":"call_049cd13b65f74d0ca27eb5b6","tool_response":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a thorough understanding of the entire system. Here is my detailed report.\n\n---\n\n## Hooks System Implementation\n\n### Registration (settings.json)\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\settings.json`\n\nEvery Claude Code lifecycle event is registered as a hook. There are 29 events (01 through 29), each mapped to a `base.sh` script in a numbered subdirectory under `.claude/hooks/`. The registration uses the Claude Code standard hook format:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"<EventName>\": [\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"\",\n        \"hooks\": [{ \"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"bash \\\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR/.claude/hooks/<NN>-<name>/base.sh\\\"\" }]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nAll matchers are empty (`\"\"`), meaning every event fires unconditionally. The event names and their corresponding directory numbers:\n\n| # | Event Name | Directory |\n|---|-----------|-----------|\n| 01 | SessionStart | 01-session-start |\n| 02 | Setup | 02-setup |\n| 03 | UserPromptSubmit | 03-user-prompt-submit |\n| 04 | UserPromptExpansion | 04-user-prompt-expansion |\n| 05 | PreToolUse | 05-pre-tool-use |\n| 06 | PermissionRequest | 06-permission-request |\n| 07 | PermissionDenied | 07-permission-denied |\n| 08 | PostToolUse | 08-post-tool-use |\n| 09 | PostToolUseFailure | 09-post-tool-use-failure |\n| 10 | PostToolBatch | 10-post-tool-batch |\n| 11 | Notification | 11-notification |\n| 12 | SubagentStart | 12-subagent-start |\n| 13 | SubagentStop | 13-subagent-stop |\n| 14 | TaskCreated | 14-task-created |\n| 15 | TaskCompleted | 15-task-completed |\n| 16 | Stop | 16-stop |\n| 17 | StopFailure | 17-stop-failure |\n| 18 | TeammateIdle | 18-teammate-idle |\n| 19 | InstructionsLoaded | 19-instructions-loaded |\n| 20 | ConfigChange | 20-config-change |\n| 21 | CwdChanged | 21-cwd-changed |\n| 22 | FileChanged | 22-file-changed |\n| 23 | WorktreeCreate | 23-worktree-create |\n| 24 | WorktreeRemove | 24-worktree-remove |\n| 25 | PreCompact | 25-pre-compact |\n| 26 | PostCompact | 26-post-compact |\n| 27 | Elicitation | 27-elicitation |\n| 28 | ElicitationResult | 28-elicitation-result |\n| 29 | SessionEnd | 29-session-end |\n\n### Hook Base Infrastructure\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\hooks\\base.sh`\n\nThis is sourced by every `base.sh` script. It provides:\n\n1. **Platform detection** -- sources `platform.sh` which detects OS type (linux/macos/windows) and resolves the Python command path.\n\n2. **Stdin JSON reading** -- `HOOK_INPUT=$(cat)` reads the full JSON payload from stdin.\n\n3. **Date-based logging** -- writes to `.claude/hooks/logs/YYYY-MM-DD.log` with `[timestamp] [LEVEL] [EventName] message` format.\n\n4. **JSON parsing** (`json_get`) -- three-tier fallback strategy:\n   - **jq** if available (fastest, most reliable)\n   - **Python** via `json_get.py` helper if Python is available\n   - **Pure sed** as last resort (only extracts top-level `\"key\": \"value\"` patterns)\n\n5. **Output function** (`hook_output`) -- takes exit code and JSON body, logs it, writes to stdout, and exits. Exit code 2 can block/modify behavior for certain events (e.g., PreToolUse can return `deny`).\n\n6. **Skill-aware dispatching** (`dispatch_to_skill`) -- looks up the current session's active skill from `.active` file, maps event numbers to script names (e.g., `05` -> `05PreToolUse`), and executes `<skill-dir>/scripts/<EventName>.sh` if it exists.\n\n### Platform Detection\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\hooks\\platform.sh`\n\nUses `uname -s` to classify into `linux`, `macos`, or `windows` (MINGW/MSYS/CYGWIN). Resolves Python path by checking: (1) embedded Python at `.claude/localLanguage/python/...`, (2) system `python3`, (3) system `python`.\n\n### Key Hook Scripts\n\n**01-session-start/base.sh** (`D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\hooks\\01-session-start\\base.sh`):\n- Triggers `init.sh` on first run (checks `.initialized` marker)\n- On every session: ensures UTF-8 encoding, checks Python availability, verifies directory integrity\n- Runs per-skill `init_check.sh` scripts for health checks\n\n**03-user-prompt-submit/base.sh** (`D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\hooks\\03-user-prompt-submit\\base.sh`):\n- Calls `skill-inject.sh` which is the **skill activation entry point**\n- If a skill matches, the skill's `03UserPromptSubmit.sh` output replaces the hook's response, injecting `additionalContext` into the prompt\n\n**05-pre-tool-use/base.sh** (`D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\hooks\\05-pre-tool-use\\base.sh`):\n- Two-layer enforcement:\n  - **Layer A**: `enforce_boundary.sh` -- reads the active skill's `SKILL.md` frontmatter `allowed-tools` list. If a tool is not in the whitelist, returns `deny`.\n  - **Layer B**: `dispatch_to_skill \"05\"` -- delegates to the skill's `05PreToolUse.sh` for skill-specific tool interception.\n\n**16-stop/base.sh** (`D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\hooks\\16-stop\\base.sh`):\n- Runs `skill-register.sh` to auto-discover new skills (scans directories for `SKILL.md`)\n- Runs the active skill's `16Stop.sh` for cleanup (removes session from `.active`)\n\n---\n\n## Skill System Implementation\n\n### Registry\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\skills\\registry.conf`\n\nA plain text file listing one skill name per line. Used by `skill-inject.sh` for matching. Skills are auto-registered by `skill-register.sh` (called at Stop event), which scans `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` directories.\n\nCurrent registered skills: `001-testcode-python`, `002-otherdoc`, `003-1-issue-init`, `003-2-issue`, `003-3-issue-discuss`, `003-4-issue-claim`, `003-5-issue-fix`, `003-6-issue-done`, `003-7-issue-pr`, `003-8-issue-test`, `003-9-issue-review`, `004-git-push`, `005-git-commit`.\n\n### Skill Activation Flow (skill-inject.sh)\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\hooks\\03-user-prompt-submit\\skill-inject.sh`\n\n1. Checks if user prompt starts with `/`\n2. Extracts skill name (text between `/` and first space)\n3. Extracts arguments (text after first space)\n4. Matches against `registry.conf` using `awk` exact match\n5. If matched, executes `<skill>/scripts/03UserPromptSubmit.sh` which returns a JSON hook response with `additionalContext`\n6. Registers the skill as active via `active_add(session_id, skill_name)`\n7. Returns metadata line (`skill_name|args`) followed by the context JSON\n\n### Active Skill Tracking (active.sh)\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\skills\\active.sh`\n\nManages the `.active` file (format: `session_id|skill_name`, one per line). Operations:\n- `active_add(sid, skill_name)` -- idempotent add/update with file locking\n- `active_remove(sid)` -- remove by session ID\n- `active_get(sid)` -- lookup skill name for a session\n- `active_remove_by_skill(skill_name)` -- remove all entries for a skill\n- `active_skills()` -- list unique skill names\n- `active_list()` -- dump all entries\n\n### Locking (lock.sh)\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\skills\\lock.sh`\n\nUses `mkdir` as an atomic cross-platform lock primitive. Features:\n- `lock_acquire(lock_dir, timeout)` -- blocking with configurable timeout (default 10s), 1-second polling interval\n- Zombie detection: if lock is older than 60 seconds, force-remove it\n- `lock_release()` -- removes the lock directory\n- Global `_LOCK_DIR` variable tracks the current lock\n\nThe `active.sh` module uses this lock with the file `.claude/skills/.active.lock`.\n\n### Skill Logging (log.sh)\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\skills\\log.sh`\n\nDual-destination logging:\n- **Unified log**: `.claude/hooks/logs/YYYY-MM-DD.log` (same as hook logs)\n- **Module log**: `.claude/skills/log/<skill-tag>/YYYY-MM-DD.log` (per-skill)\n\nUsage pattern: set `SKILL_TAG` before sourcing, then call `skill_log \"LEVEL\" \"message\"`.\n\n### Tool Boundary Enforcement (enforce_boundary.sh)\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\skills\\enforce_boundary.sh`\n\nReads the active skill's `SKILL.md` YAML frontmatter, extracts the `allowed-tools` list, and denies any tool not in the whitelist. If no whitelist is defined, everything is allowed. This runs in the PreToolUse hook before skill-specific dispatching.\n\n### Skill Directory Structure\n\nEach skill follows this pattern:\n\n```\n.claude/skills/<skill-name>/\n  SKILL.md              # Definition with YAML frontmatter (name, description, allowed-tools)\n  scripts/\n    init.sh             # First-time setup (called by init.sh on first run)\n    init_check.sh       # Per-session health check (called by 01-session-start)\n    03UserPromptSubmit.sh  # Context injection when skill is activated\n    16Stop.sh           # Cleanup when Claude finishes (removes session from .active)\n```\n\nOptional lifecycle scripts that can be added: `05PreToolUse.sh`, `08PostToolUse.sh`, `29SessionEnd.sh`, etc. (any event from the dispatch table in `base.sh`).\n\nThe `03UserPromptSubmit.sh` script is the **context injection point** -- it outputs a JSON hook response like:\n```json\n{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"additionalContext\":\"<dynamic context>\"}}\n```\n\nThe `16Stop.sh` script is the **cleanup point** -- it calls `active_remove(session_id)` to clear the session from `.active`.\n\n### SKILL.md Frontmatter\n\nExample from `002-otherdoc`:\n```yaml\n---\nname: 002-otherdoc\ndescription: ...\nuser-invocable: true\nallowed-tools:\n  - Bash\n  - Read\n  - Write\n  - Edit\n  - Glob\n  - Grep\n---\n```\n\nThe `allowed-tools` field is consumed by `enforce_boundary.sh`. The `user-invocable` flag marks it as a slash-command skill. `skill-register.sh` uses the presence of `SKILL.md` as the indicator that a directory is a valid skill.\n\n---\n\n## Init System\n\n### init.sh\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\init.sh`\n\nRuns once (guarded by `.claude/.initialized` marker). Steps:\n\n1. **Directory creation** -- calls `ensure_dirs.sh` to create all dirs from `dirs.conf`, plus creates today's `doc/otherDoc/YYYY-MM-DD/`\n2. **Platform detection** -- sources `platform.sh`\n3. **Python environment** -- calls `ensure_python.sh` which uses a multi-strategy approach: embedded Python > system Python > auto-download (with 5-attempt limit, state tracked in `.python-state`)\n4. **UTF-8 configuration** -- writes OS-appropriate locale settings to `~/.bashrc` (with idempotency markers)\n5. **Per-skill init** -- runs each skill's `scripts/init.sh` (non-blocking)\n6. **Marker file** -- writes `.initialized` with JSON metadata (os, python path, utf8 status, timestamp)\n\n### dirs.conf\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\dirs.conf`\n\nFormat: `<relative-path>  <description>`. Defines project directories that must exist:\n- `doc/testcode/python/api`\n- `doc/testcode/python/other`\n- `doc/otherDoc`\n- `doc/issues/drafts`\n- `doc/issues/templates`\n\n### ensure_dirs.sh\n\nFile: `D:\\development\\code\\opencode\\claude-hk\\.claude\\scripts\\ensure_dirs.sh`\n\nThree functions:\n- `ensure_all_dirs(log_file)` -- reads `dirs.conf`, creates missing dirs, returns JSON stats\n- `ensure_skill_dirs(keyword)` -- creates only dirs whose path contains the keyword\n- `check_dirs()` -- reports missing dirs without creating them (returns \"ALL OK\" or \"MISSING: path\")\n\n---\n\n## Complete Lifecycle Summary\n\n1. **First session**: `01-session-start` -> `init.sh` -> creates dirs, configures Python/UTF-8, runs skill inits, writes `.initialized`\n2. **Every session start**: `01-session-start` -> ensures UTF-8/Python/dirs, runs skill `init_check.sh`\n3. **User types `/skillname args`**: `03-user-prompt-submit` -> `skill-inject.sh` -> matches registry -> runs skill's `03UserPromptSubmit.sh` -> injects `additionalContext` into prompt -> registers session in `.active`\n4. **Every tool call**: `05-pre-tool-use` -> `enforce_boundary.sh` (whitelist check) -> `dispatch_to_skill(\"05\")` (skill-specific interception)\n5. **Claude finishes**: `16-stop` -> `skill-register.sh` (auto-discover new skills) -> skill's `16Stop.sh` (removes session from `.active`)\n6. **Other events** (04, 06-15, 17-29): all `base.sh` scripts source the shared `base.sh`, enabling `dispatch_to_skill()` for any event where a skill has a corresponding script"}]}]}
